{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791397745,"nonce":"i4rJ/67FqDwyV+rR1LDfEPPCej4=","title":"OSR: LLVM vector live-ins must use frame-slot alignment","message":"The shared integer counter vectorizer exposes a cross-tier ABI defect: OsrFrame aligns vectors to their element alignment (8 bytes for i64x2); LLVM compile_osr_helper emits default-aligned vector loads (16 bytes). The mixed vector/scalar frame places vector slots at offsets 0x28, 0x48 and 0x68. NUC gdb confirms SIGSEGV in the LLVM resume helper at vmovdqa 0x28(%rdi), with a 16-byte-aligned frame base. Native/standalone vector functions and ordinary conformance pass; the crash requires actual promotion/OSR with vector live-ins.\n\nReproducer: new shared vector-counter candidate from issue 2e204d81c82ef9159df9e293cafc27026b4e52b4e66474269cec84635246f8ec, ZYLUA_LLVM=1 zylua run crates/zyntax_lua/benchmarks/inlined_call.lua. Trace /tmp/zyntax-counter-llvm-crash.trace and debugger evidence /tmp/zyntax-counter-crash-gdb.log on NUC.\n\nLoad frame slots using the shared frame ABI alignment, including ordinary live-ins, phi seeds and region re-entry. Preserve the ABI layout; do not claim unsupported 16-byte alignment. Add mixed scalar/vector helper and native transfer regressions before accepting the HIR optimization.","files":null}]}